WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.736
AgentWorkShop — an industrial multi-agent platform, recorded live on a running production line.

2
00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:21.136
Every line, every signal, one control room. Hardware in, decisions out — and nothing leaves the governed path.

3
00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:30.400
Live telemetry, six field protocols — every sample stamped with its batch, recipe and line.

4
00:00:32.420 --> 00:00:37.836
The new E D A pipeline. Pull live data — or bring your own table.

5
00:00:38.106 --> 00:00:45.466
Shape it with your own code: filters, aggregates, derived columns — executed right in your browser.

6
00:00:45.736 --> 00:00:53.504
Choose a chart, tune the fields, save the whole recipe as a template. New data, one click, re-plotted.

7
00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:14.232
Every tool is catalogued with its source, the roles allowed to call it, and the channels that scoped it down.

8
00:01:14.502 --> 00:01:21.358
Agents propose. The platform verifies against bound nodes and live grants. You decide.

9
00:01:21.628 --> 00:01:27.620
Every call is rate-limited, checked and journaled — by design, not by policy.

10
00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:37.552
Ontology makes the plant machine-readable — entities, relations and rules, each bound to a real node.

11
00:01:37.822 --> 00:01:45.422
Models learn from the line, then serve optimization through a guarded solver. Nothing is trusted until it passes.

12
00:01:45.692 --> 00:01:51.036
And a solver cross-checks every recommendation against the physics it learned from.

13
00:01:51.306 --> 00:01:58.906
Published as a versioned release, every entity, relation and rule carries its evidence and a content hash.

14
00:02:02.930 --> 00:02:08.346
Different agents, different tools, different permissions — scoped down to the node.

15
00:02:08.616 --> 00:02:14.680
Four teams share one line, each with its own scenario, tools and evidence trail.

16
00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:24.852
Protocols, analyses, twins — all plugins. The diagnostics bridge and knowledge base plug in the same way.

17
00:02:26.870 --> 00:02:34.710
In one live batch, every setpoint was acknowledged and read back; a step-limited request was correctly rejected.

18
00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:38.716
Data, decision, action — with proof.

19
00:02:41.740 --> 00:02:48.548
Every chart is a saved, reusable view — owned, versioned, and shareable with the team.

20
00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:55.770
AgentWorkShop. Open source, plugin-ready, built for the shop floor.
